  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-30T21:32:12.81Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "PG0CY6A6oKSkpxKTTl/VmfF/WsuBdQgYWtOTswFqY87S7DDbYvMGDrVc6SRpoH6cgGI0vhBywcADx8hSGmFuog==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 668361,
  "published": "2026-10-30T21:06:55.653Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.9.0: what the issued token carries, and the decision point's question for another user. MyIdentityJwtTokenResult gains SecurityStamp and UserId, read from the claims the token is signed with, so a refresh token of your own binds to the stamp without parsing the JWT; the claim's name is published as MyIdentityClaimTypes.SecurityStamp, same value. New IMyIdentityPermissionAdminService.HasPermissionForUserAsync answers HasPermissionAsync's question for another user, from their stored roles with the decision point's own rules, behind both the role-assignment and the role-configuration read gates, confined to the caller's tenant. A class of your own that implements IMyIdentityPermissionAdminService gains a member to implement; nothing else breaks. The package validation baseline is 5.8.0. Upgrading from 5.8.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §53.",
